# netsurf: history -- kept across runs, on the home page and its own page
# (patch 232; roadmap WS-E, Phase 1 exit)
# Generated 2026-10-10
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 231)
#
# The core records every page a window shows in its URL database (title,
# visit count, last visit), but leaves loading and saving it to the
# frontend, and the Vita did neither: no history, not even within a run,
# and nothing kept between runs. The home page was also written once at
# start-up, so its downloads list went stale as soon as one finished.
#
#  - vita/main.c: urldb_load(ux0:data/VitaBrowser/urldb) at start (before
#    the cookie jar), urldb_save() whenever the cookie jar is saved (after
#    a page loads, at most every VITA_COOKIE_SAVE_MS -- the PS button
#    skips exit code) and at quit. The core drops pages not visited for
#    expire_url days (28) when it saves. START now rewrites the home page
#    before going there.
#  - vita/chrome.c: the home page gets "Recently visited" (the 8 newest
#    visits: title, host, "5 min ago") and an "All history" link; the
#    history page (ux0:data/VitaBrowser/history.html, written with the
#    home page) lists up to 200, newest first. Our own pages (home,
#    history, downloads under ux0:data/VitaBrowser/) and about: pages are
#    left out. Ages, not clock times: the Vita's clock zone is unknown,
#    a difference reads right in every zone.
#  - vita/interact.c: A_WAIT (visit times are whole seconds, so the step
#    before IN-download waits 1.1 s to keep the newest visit unambiguous)
#    and C_HISTORY: after START, the home page's recent list must start
#    with IN-download.html (the last page visited) and the history page
#    must hold at least 8 pages; then the history page is opened.
#
